# Brood source (.blsp) is a Lisp; until Brood is its own Linguist language,
# highlight it as Clojure — the closest common grammar (handles [] vectors,
# {} maps, and :keywords, all of which Brood uses).
# linguist-detectable=false keeps .blsp out of the repo language stats (this is
# a Rust implementation of a Lisp, not a Clojure project) while still applying
# the grammar for highlighting.
*.blsp linguist-language=Clojure linguist-detectable=false

# The append-only logs: parallel sessions each add an entry at the bottom, and a plain
# merge then conflicts on every pair of pushes (three times on 2026-11-25 alone). A union
# merge keeps both sides' lines, which for an entry appended at the end is exactly right;
# an edit to an EARLIER entry on both sides is still worth reading in the diff, and
# `doc_refs` refuses a duplicate ADR number, so a collision is caught, not silently kept.
docs/devlog.md merge=union
docs/decisions/adr-*.md merge=union
docs/known-issues.md merge=union
